  "final_answer_preview": "To potentially avoid punishment after committing theft, it is crucial to consider the circumstances of the offense. If the value of the stolen property is less than five thousand rupees and it is a first-time offense, returning the stolen property or its value may result in a punishment of community service instead of imprisonment. This is outlined in Section 303(2) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. However, if the theft involved preparation for causing harm or restraint, as described in Section 307, the penalties are significantly harsher, including rigorous imprisonment for up to ten years. Therefore, the nature of the theft and the actions taken post-offense are critical in determining the possibility of avoiding punishment.",
